  "chat": [
    {
      "r": "user",
      "t": "Let’s build STATIC: Joe wakes up, his parents are changing, and the TV keeps saying the world is normal."
    },
    {
      "r": "bot",
      "t": "The sample contains <b>12 shots / 45 seconds</b>, nested Film / Act / Scene / Beat / Shot scopes, a lined script and production references."
    },
    {
      "r": "user",
      "t": "The family wide needs to feel ritualistic. Keep them dead-center on the sofa."
    },
    {
      "r": "bot",
      "t": "<b>Shot 2</b> is the symmetrical family wide with Pete and Donna. The character-consistency board is an Explore reference; no generation was run."
    },
    {
      "r": "user",
      "t": "Keep the transformation quiet rather than monstrous."
    },
    {
      "r": "bot",
      "t": "<b>Shot 5</b> is Pete’s cheek turning to wool. The VFX breakdown remains a planning document, not a shot or a background plate."
    },
    {
      "r": "user",
      "t": "Show the reveal options."
    },
    {
      "r": "bot",
      "t": "<b>Shot 9</b> has a circled source still and a same-source framing study at Shot / Footage. These are not rendered alternate video takes."
    },
    {
      "r": "user",
      "t": "Show the 15-second trailer."
    },
    {
      "r": "bot",
      "t": "<b>Trailer C</b>: Joe wake-up (1), morph detail (5), broken CRT (7), then the white street (9), <b>15 seconds</b>. Switch cuts with the timeline name. Festival Master E is a deliverable of Picture Lock A."
    }
  ],
